              "id": "c6d5face-bdd3-3523-9769-156a07ab4266",
              "name": "Potential ReDoS Vulnerability Due to RegExp() Function Argument 'a' in Application: Recommended Use of Hardcoded Regexes and Input Validation or Regex Checking/Sanitization Libraries",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe code snippet provided is vulnerable to a Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) attack. This vulnerability occurs when the application uses user input directly in a Regular Expression (RegExp) without proper sanitization or validation. An attacker can provide a specially crafted input that causes the regular expression engine to consume excessive resources, leading to a denial of service.\n\nIn the provided code, the user input `a.namespace` is used directly in a RegExp, which can lead to a ReDoS attack if the input is not properly validated or sanitized.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to:\n\n1. Avoid using user input directly in regular expressions. If it is necessary, ensure the input is properly validated and sanitized before use.\n2. Use hardcoded regular expressions where possible, as they are less likely to be vulnerable to ReDoS attacks.\n3. Consider using a library or tool that can check or sanitize regular expressions to prevent ReDoS attacks.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nThe following code snippet demonstrates how to sanitize the user input before using it in a RegExp:\n\n```javascript\nif(a.namespace) {\n    var sanitizedInput = a.namespace.replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9\\.]/g, ''); // sanitize user input\n    A=RegExp(\"(^|\\\\.)\"+sanitizedInput.split(\".\").join(\"\\\\.(?:.*\\\\.)?\")+\"(\\\\.|$)\");\n}\n```\n\nIn this code, the `replace` function is used to remove any characters from the user input that are not alphanumeric or a period. This sanitized input is then used in the RegExp.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code snippet appears to be using jQuery, as indicated by the use of the `$` function and the `.closest` method.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP ReDoS](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Regular_expression_Denial_of_Service_-_ReDoS)\n- [CWE-400: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/400.html)"
              },
