            {
              "id": "7eb4d53d-0b7f-37cc-98bd-356954da857e",
              "name": "High-Risk Dockerfile Vulnerability: Lack of Non-Root User Specification",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe \"High-Risk Dockerfile Vulnerability: Lack of Non-Root User Specification\" is a security vulnerability in Docker where the Dockerfile does not specify a non-root user for running the container. This means that the Docker container runs with root privileges by default. If an attacker manages to break out of the container, they would have root access to the host system, which is a significant security risk.\n\n## Security Concern\n\nRunning Docker containers as root is a security concern because it provides the container with potentially dangerous permissions. If an attacker manages to exploit a vulnerability within the container, they could gain root access to the host system. This would allow them to execute arbitrary commands, modify system files, and potentially take over the entire system.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to always run Docker containers as a non-root user. This can be done by specifying a non-root user in the Dockerfile using the `USER` directive. If the application running inside the container requires certain permissions, these should be granted explicitly and in a controlled manner.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is a fix for the provided Dockerfile:\n\n```Dockerfile\nFROM tutum/lamp:latest\n\n# Create a new user and group 'appuser'\nRUN groupadd -r appuser && useradd -r -g appuser appuser\n\n# Switch to 'appuser'\nUSER appuser\n```\n\nThis Dockerfile creates a new user and group named 'appuser', and then switches to this user using the `USER` directive. Now, the Docker container will run as 'appuser' instead of root.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided Dockerfile is based on the `tutum/lamp:latest` image, which includes Apache, MySQL, and PHP. Therefore, no additional library dependencies are required.\n\n## References\n\n- [CWE-250: Execution with Unnecessary Privileges](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/250.html)"
              },
