            {
              "id": "db1e365a-dc6b-3d26-acf9-a936e7084052",
              "name": "Prototype Pollution Vulnerability Detected",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nPrototype Pollution is a vulnerability that occurs when the properties of JavaScript's object prototype can be modified by the control of an attacker. This can occur when an application allows an attacker to manipulate the properties of JavaScript objects. When the application processes the malicious object, the attacker can modify the application's behavior or even achieve Remote Code Execution.\n\nIn the provided code, the vulnerability can occur if the input parameters `a`, `b`, `d`, `e` are controlled by an attacker and are not properly sanitized before being processed.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to:\n\n- Avoid using user input directly in the application's logic.\n- Validate and sanitize user input before processing it.\n- Use a well-maintained library that is designed to handle user input safely.\n- Regularly update and patch all components of the application.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nWithout the full context of the code, it's hard to provide a specific fix. However, a general recommendation would be to sanitize the input parameters `a`, `b`, `d`, `e` before they are processed. This could be done using a function like this:\n\n```javascript\nfunction sanitizeInput(input) {\n    // Implement input sanitization logic here\n    return sanitizedInput;\n}\n```\n\nAnd then use this function to sanitize the inputs:\n\n```javascript\nc.fn[a]=function(d,e){\n    a = sanitizeInput(a);\n    d = sanitizeInput(d);\n    e = sanitizeInput(e);\n    // Rest of the code\n}\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code seems to be using jQuery, but without the full context, it's hard to determine if there are other dependencies.\n\n## References\n\n- [CWE-250: Execution with Unnecessary Privileges](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/250.html)\n\nPlease note that the links were active and accessible at the time of writing this report."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
