              "id": "8d1bf387-6e22-363a-adde-ec3a162b9bb9",
              "name": "XSS Vulnerability from User-Controlled Data in HTML String",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe provided JavaScript code is vulnerable to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attacks due to the use of user-controlled data in an HTML string. This vulnerability arises when the application includes untrusted data in a new HTML string used to generate a page. An attacker can inject malicious scripts into the HTML string, which will be executed when the page is rendered by the browser.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to:\n\n1. Avoid inserting untrusted data directly into the HTML document.\n2. Use safe JavaScript APIs, such as `element.textContent` (not `element.innerHTML`), or use functions in JavaScript frameworks that automatically escape for you.\n3. If you have to insert untrusted data into HTML, always sanitize it first using a trusted library or built-in browser functions.\n4. Implement a strong Content Security Policy (CSP) to reduce the impact of any XSS vulnerabilities.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nThe specific vulnerability sink in the provided code is the line:\n\n```javascript\nc.innerHTML=\"x<style>\"+b+\"</style>\"\n```\n\nThis line can be fixed by escaping the user-controlled data `b` before inserting it into the HTML string. Here is a simple fix using the `encodeURI` function:\n\n```javascript\nc.innerHTML=\"x<style>\"+encodeURI(b)+\"</style>\"\n```\n\nHowever, this is a simple fix and may not cover all edge cases. It is recommended to use a comprehensive HTML sanitization library for this purpose.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code does not appear to have any external library dependencies.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP XSS (Cross Site Scripting) Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP DOM based XSS Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/DOM_based_XSS_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)"
