            {
              "id": "cbd10c25-cafd-30ab-8073-a5f5acdd680e",
              "name": "Secure Regex Against User Input to Prevent ReDoS Vulnerability",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) is a type of Denial of Service attack. Many Regular Expressions implementations may reach extreme situations that cause them to work very slowly (exponentially related to input size). An attacker can then cause a program using a Regular Expression to enter these extreme situations and then hang for a very long time.\n\nIn JavaScript, this vulnerability can occur when user input is passed into a regular expression without proper sanitization. This can lead to a situation where the regular expression takes a very long time to evaluate, effectively causing a denial of service.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should avoid using user input inside a regular expression without proper sanitization. If you must use user input in a regular expression, make sure to sanitize the input to ensure it does not cause the regular expression to enter a state that would take a long time to evaluate.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nThe provided code does not seem to contain a regular expression, so it's hard to provide a specific fix. However, here is a general example of how to sanitize user input before using it in a regular expression:\n\n```javascript\nlet userInput = getUserInput();\nlet sanitizedInput = userInput.replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9]/g, '');\nlet regex = new RegExp(sanitizedInput);\n```\n\nIn this example, `getUserInput()` is a hypothetical function that gets user input. The `replace` function is used to remove any non-alphanumeric characters from the user input before it is used in the regular expression.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code seems to be using jQuery, so jQuery would be a required library dependency.\n\n## OWASP and CWE Resources\n\n- [OWASP ReDoS](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Regular_expression_Denial_of_Service_-_ReDoS)\n- [CWE-400: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/400.html)\n\nPlease note that the links were active and accessible at the time of writing this report."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-400",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/400.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-400"
                ]
              }
