            {
              "id": "ac56a578-df43-3f8a-8648-c88364854c00",
              "name": "\"Vulnerability in Dynamic Execution with Eval and Function\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe vulnerability in dynamic execution with `eval` and `Function` in JavaScript is a serious security issue. It arises when user input is directly passed into `eval()` or `Function()` functions. These functions execute the code they are passed with the privileges of the caller. If you run `eval()` with a string that could be affected by a malicious user, you may end up running malicious code on the user's machine with the permissions of your webpage / extension.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nAvoid using `eval()` or the `Function()` constructor. If you have to use them, make sure the string being passed to them is not affected by user input. If user input must be executed, it should be first sanitized and validated to ensure it does not contain any malicious code.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nThe specific vulnerability sink in the provided code is the `(new Function(\"return \"+j))()` part. This can be fixed by avoiding the use of `Function()` constructor and using `JSON.parse()` instead.\n\nReplace:\n\n```javascript\nreturn E.JSON&&E.JSON.parse?E.JSON.parse(j):(new Function(\"return \"+j))();\n```\n\nWith:\n\n```javascript\nreturn E.JSON&&E.JSON.parse?E.JSON.parse(j):null;\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example does not seem to have any specific library dependencies.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP - Code Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Code_Injection)\n- [CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-94",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-94"
                ]
