            {
              "id": "f5612b63-3e63-35ed-a97f-6cbe82fe38f8",
              "name": "Potential XSS Vulnerability from User-Controlled Data in HTML String",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe \"Potential XSS Vulnerability from User-Controlled Data in HTML String\" vulnerability in JavaScript refers to a situation where an attacker can inject malicious scripts into web pages viewed by other users. This is possible when a web application uses input from an HTTP request directly within HTML output without properly sanitizing the user-controlled data. This can lead to a Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attack, which is a type of injection, in which malicious scripts are injected into otherwise benign and trusted websites.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to:\n\n1. **Escape User Input**: Always escape user-controlled data before displaying it in HTML. This can prevent most XSS attacks as it ensures that the user input is not interpreted as code.\n\n2. **Use Secure Libraries**: Use libraries that automatically escape user input, such as ReactJS.\n\n3. **Content Security Policy (CSP)**: Implement a Content Security Policy (CSP). It's a security layer that helps to detect and mitigate certain types of attacks, including XSS.\n\n4. **Input Validation**: Validate and sanitize user input to ensure it conforms to the expected format.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nThe provided code snippet is incomplete and does not clearly indicate where the user-controlled data is being used in an HTML string. However, a general fix would involve using the `textContent` property instead of `innerHTML` when inserting text from user input into an HTML element, or using a function like `encodeURI()` or `encodeURIComponent()` to sanitize user input that will be included in an HTML string.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code snippet appears to be using the jQuery library.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP XSS Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP DOM based XSS Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/DOM_based_XSS_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-79",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-79"
                ]
              }
