            {
              "id": "143dc4f4-40c4-3f03-8176-8ec45197b107",
              "name": "\"Logging Errors for Debugging and Security Monitoring to Prevent Silent Error Suppression by Empty Catch Block\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe vulnerability in question is related to the improper handling of errors in JavaScript. Specifically, it pertains to the use of empty catch blocks that suppress errors, making them \"silent\". This can lead to a variety of issues, including the inability to debug problems effectively and potential security risks, as malicious actors may exploit these silent errors to their advantage.\n\nIn the provided code snippet, the catch block is empty, which means that any exceptions that occur when trying to remove an event from an element are simply ignored. This can lead to unexpected behavior and potential security vulnerabilities.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to always handle exceptions in a meaningful way. This can include logging the error, displaying a user-friendly error message, or even re-throwing the exception to be handled at a higher level. Ignoring exceptions should be avoided, as it can lead to unexpected behavior and potential security vulnerabilities.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nA simple fix for the provided code snippet would be to log the error to the console:\n\n```javascript\nc.each(\"blur focus focusin focusout load resize scroll unload click dblclick mousedown mouseup mousemove mouseover mouseout mouseenter mouseleave change select submit keydown keypress keyup error\".split(\" \"),function(a,b){c.fn[b]=function(d,e){if(e==null){e=d;d=null}return arguments.length>0?this.bind(b,d,e):this.trigger(b)};if(c.attrFn)c.attrFn[b]=true});E.attachEvent&&!E.addEventListener&&c(E).bind(\"unload\",function(){for(var a in c.cache)if(c.cache[a].handle)try{c.event.remove(c.cache[a].handle.elem)}catch(b){console.error(b)}});\n\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code snippet appears to depend on the jQuery library.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Top 10 - A6:2017-Security Misconfiguration](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/2017/A6_2017-Security_Misconfiguration)\n- [CWE-390: Detection of Error Condition Without Action](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/390.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-390",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/390.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-390"
                ]
              }
